
------------------------------------------------
Add an External Tool in IntelliJ

If you do this often, you can add a menu item:

Settings → Tools → External Tools
Click +.
Configure:
Name: Open in Thunar
Program: thunar
Arguments: $ProjectFileDir$
Working directory: $ProjectFileDir$

Then you can access it from Tools → External Tools → Open in Thunar, and it will open the current project's folder directly in the XFCE file manager.
--------------------------------------------------
Format the current file
Linux/Windows: Ctrl + Alt + L
macOS: ⌥ Option + ⌘ Command + L
